  {
   "t": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 762,
   "w": 534,
   "h": 27,
   "html": "<h3>Hello, this is my sixth week of the Scad x Harbor blog!</h3>",
   "plain": "Hello, this is my sixth week of the Scad x Harbor blog!",
   "head": true
  },
  {
   "t": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 800,
   "w": 285,
   "h": 27,
   "html": "<h3>Feedback From Mentors:</h3>",
   "plain": "Feedback From Mentors:",
   "head": true
  },
  {
   "t": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 838,
   "w": 930,
   "h": 581,
   "html": "<p>Vi:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: sharp the watch; light more dramatic</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 5: Gears</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 6&mdash;the reveal&mdash;use lighting to lead to the final reveal</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Hailey:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>reframe better; watch out for harsh edges</li>\n\t<li>shot 5: Get more light on gears</li>\n\t<li>shot 6&mdash;still tight *</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Emma:​pam</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>shot 6: Hold and pull out</li>\n\t<li>shot 4: overlit</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Billy:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Background out of focus</li>\n\t<li>Don&#39;t render with depth of field</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Molly:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4&mdash;needs to be longer</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: subtle push into the watch and then push out&mdash;the camera can tie it together </p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: lighting feeling flat/edge light picking up the bevel</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 5: no glass being picked up/animated a card</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 6: speed upstart and then have some time to settle on watch</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: The background is dark</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4/5&mdash;transition needs work</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>​</p>\n\n<p>​</p>",
   "plain": "Vi:\n\n\n\t\n\tshot 4: sharp the watch; light more dramatic\n\t\n\t\n\tshot 5: Gears\n\t\n\t\n\tsh",
   "head": false
  },
  {
   "t": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 838,
   "w": 930,
   "h": 581,
   "html": "<p>Vi:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: sharp the watch; light more dramatic</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 5: Gears</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 6&mdash;the reveal&mdash;use lighting to lead to the final reveal</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Hailey:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>reframe better; watch out for harsh edges</li>\n\t<li>shot 5: Get more light on gears</li>\n\t<li>shot 6&mdash;still tight *</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Emma:​pam</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>shot 6: Hold and pull out</li>\n\t<li>shot 4: overlit</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Billy:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Background out of focus</li>\n\t<li>Don&#39;t render with depth of field</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Molly:​</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4&mdash;needs to be longer</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: subtle push into the watch and then push out&mdash;the camera can tie it together </p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: lighting feeling flat/edge light picking up the bevel</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 5: no glass being picked up/animated a card</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 6: speed upstart and then have some time to settle on watch</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4: The background is dark</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>\n\t<p>shot 4/5&mdash;transition needs work</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>​</p>\n\n<p>​</p>",
   "plain": "Vi:\n\n\n\t\n\tshot 4: sharp the watch; light more dramatic\n\t\n\t\n\tshot 5: Gears\n\t\n\t\n\tsh",
   "head": false
